From 710bf7329abf86e37db529f19c8f394099238892 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krishna Chaitanya Chundru <krishna.chundru@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:07:43 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] bus: mhi: host: pci_generic: Add DUN channel configuration

Add the DUN uplink (ch32) and downlink (ch33) channel definitions to
the Qualcomm modem MHI channel configuration table.

These channels are used for transporting AT commands over MHI.
Defining them allows the MHI core to create the corresponding DUN MHI
devices and enables userspace access to the modem AT interface through
the MHI WWAN client driver.

Signed-off-by: Krishna Chaitanya Chundru <krishna.chundru@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Manivannan Sadhasivam <manivannan.sadhasivam@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260925-mhi_dun-v1-1-65bc07ec8a59@oss.qualcomm.com

Backported for 6.18 (commit 710bf7329abf, identical change).

LOCAL commentary, not part of the upstream commit message - why this board needs
it and how it was confirmed, kept because it is the evidence this port rests on:

The generic modem_qcom_v1 config is what the Quectel RG520N-EB binds: it
enumerates as the plain Qualcomm 17cb:0308 and so falls through to
mhi_qcom_sdx65_info, which declared DIAG/MBIM/QMI/IPCR/IP_SW0/IP_HW0/FIREHOSE
but no DUN - so the host never opened MHI channel 32/33 and no AT port appeared
on the router, while every other modem profile in this file (Quectel em1xx/rm5xx,
Telit, Sierra, Foxconn) already carried DUN at 32/33.

The modem firmware does provide it: verified on the RG520N-EB (sdxlemur) over
adb, which runs `port_bridge smd7 mhi_pipe_32` - the modem bridges its AT port
(smd7) to MHI channel 32 and merely waits for the host to open it (the
device-side /dev/mhi_pipe_32 is created on demand; only the channels
modem_qcom_v1 opens - 2/4/10/12/14/16 - exist until then).

mhi_wwan_ctrl maps "DUN" -> WWAN_PORT_AT, so the host exposes /dev/wwan0at0.
HW-proven on this board: the port appeared and answered AT (ATI -> Quectel
RG520N-EB) directly from the router, with no adb-into-modem detour.

Signed-off-by: Muhammad Huda Nugroho <mhudan21@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pci_generic.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pci_generic.c
@@ -314,6 +314,8 @@ static const struct mhi_channel_config modem_qcom_v1_mhi_channels[] = {
 	MHI_CHANNEL_CONFIG_DL(15, "QMI", 4, 0),
 	MHI_CHANNEL_CONFIG_UL(20, "IPCR", 8, 0),
 	MHI_CHANNEL_CONFIG_DL(21, "IPCR", 8, 0),
+	MHI_CHANNEL_CONFIG_UL(32, "DUN", 32, 0),
+	MHI_CHANNEL_CONFIG_DL(33, "DUN", 32, 0),
 	MHI_CHANNEL_CONFIG_UL_FP(34, "FIREHOSE", 32, 0),
 	MHI_CHANNEL_CONFIG_DL_FP(35, "FIREHOSE", 32, 0),
 	MHI_CHANNEL_CONFIG_UL(46, "IP_SW0", 64, 2),
